1
00:00:01,180 --> 00:00:07,080
My dear girl, how I wish I had never
brought you into this wretched world.

2
00:00:07,400 --> 00:00:10,360
Now I see that I've yet
to break free of my past.

3
00:00:10,680 --> 00:00:14,460
Cursed worm, now I'm angry!

4
00:00:19,800 --> 00:00:21,640
No, it can't!

5
00:00:25,940 --> 00:00:30,377
What was it you said about
fate you just climb am i right?

6
00:00:30,460 --> 00:00:36,220
Well i hope you like flying
instead there you go!

7
00:00:38,200 --> 00:00:39,600
Freeze!

8
00:01:11,740 --> 00:01:13,140
Let's go.

9
00:01:36,220 --> 00:01:41,920
Nell 'ingua membo, lachimmo donna Requiem

10
00:01:47,700 --> 00:01:53,037
Nessuno può succedere
un destino scelto Roman

11
00:01:53,120 --> 00:01:56,777
solo il risultato che
non sarebbe distrutto

12
00:01:56,860 --> 00:02:00,957
L 'interna Zoom esiste

13
00:02:01,040 --> 00:02:04,277
solo del me Puoi cantare

14
00:02:04,360 --> 00:02:07,000
canzoni di tristezza
The end of the season.

15
00:02:52,680 --> 00:02:55,397
To be

16
00:02:55,480 --> 00:03:02,480
continued...

17
00:03:06,000 --> 00:03:06,830
It's...

18
00:03:06,913 --> 00:03:07,743
it's her soul!

19
00:03:07,826 --> 00:03:08,680
We gotta act!

20
00:03:09,200 --> 00:03:10,030
No!

21
00:03:10,220 --> 00:03:11,100
Goddammit!

22
00:03:11,640 --> 00:03:12,980
Hey Trish!

23
00:03:13,120 --> 00:03:14,120
Get back here!

24
00:03:17,900 --> 00:03:18,780
Look!

25
00:03:19,700 --> 00:03:21,680
Now to seize my fate!

26
00:03:24,000 --> 00:03:25,176
At last you're mine!

27
00:03:25,520 --> 00:03:29,960
With this victory, fate's
designs are finally realized!

28
00:03:30,500 --> 00:03:35,260
Now behold as Emperor Crimson's
glorious ascension At last begins!

29
00:03:40,080 --> 00:03:40,910
Curses!

30
00:03:44,200 --> 00:03:45,030
Why?

31
00:03:45,113 --> 00:03:46,140
Why does it idle?

32
00:03:46,540 --> 00:03:48,020
Wait, those brats!

33
00:03:48,220 --> 00:03:49,749
What could they have done?

34
00:03:50,320 --> 00:03:52,480
Damn it, I can't grasp it!

35
00:03:53,000 --> 00:03:54,077
No, my...

36
00:03:54,160 --> 00:03:56,700
What foul affliction have you handed me?

37
00:03:57,000 --> 00:03:59,588
How could you children
have broken my grasp?

38
00:04:21,960 --> 00:04:22,790
How?

39
00:04:22,873 --> 00:04:23,980
How can this be?

40
00:04:25,340 --> 00:04:26,170
Whoa.

41
00:04:26,280 --> 00:04:28,597
Whatever had me glued
in there just went away.

42
00:04:28,680 --> 00:04:30,209
What the hell is going on?

43
00:04:30,420 --> 00:04:32,160
This wind, could it be?

44
00:04:36,620 --> 00:04:40,317
What a curious revelation, boss?

45
00:04:40,400 --> 00:04:43,137
Despite all your fervid boasting,

46
00:04:43,220 --> 00:04:47,477
those allegedly flawless
eyes didn't see this coming!

47
00:04:47,560 --> 00:04:51,117
You arrogant swine!

48
00:04:51,200 --> 00:04:54,537
Still, I must thank you—you've
shown us the path to victory.

49
00:04:54,620 --> 00:04:56,497
Requiem's power;

50
00:04:56,580 --> 00:05:01,420
its crux appears to be this luminescent
sphere floating behind each of of

51
00:05:02,680 --> 00:05:03,510
our souls.

52
00:05:03,593 --> 00:05:05,217
One need only crush it.

53
00:05:05,300 --> 00:05:08,418
Your desire for the arrow
stopped you from completely

54
00:05:09,840 --> 00:05:11,000
destroying Requiem.

55
00:05:11,500 --> 00:05:14,017
I, however, feel no such inclination.

56
00:05:14,100 --> 00:05:15,780
It would be very simple.

57
00:05:16,080 --> 00:05:18,198
I could end it all in a single blow.

58
00:05:18,520 --> 00:05:19,680
Wait, Bucciarati.

59
00:05:20,060 --> 00:05:21,178
Think for a moment.

60
00:05:21,360 --> 00:05:22,860
Is anyone worthier?

61
00:05:23,020 --> 00:05:25,860
Can you name even one person? Bucciarati.

62
00:05:26,220 --> 00:05:29,760
You know that I am
worthy of becoming king.

63
00:05:31,420 --> 00:05:32,250
Damn you!

64
00:05:32,700 --> 00:05:36,340
I will never allow your feeble
hands to touch the arrow!

65
00:05:36,740 --> 00:05:39,387
Everyone's souls will
return to their bodies.

66
00:05:40,020 --> 00:05:41,060
Post-haste!

67
00:05:49,260 --> 00:05:50,966
Look, it's rushing back here!

68
00:05:51,160 --> 00:05:53,600
Whoa, that's Trisha's soul! He's done!

69
00:05:53,820 --> 00:05:54,897
Guys, check it out!

70
00:05:54,980 --> 00:05:56,520
Blue Girardi, you did it!

71
00:05:56,780 --> 00:05:59,486
I didn't think you'd
pull it off, but you did!

72
00:06:14,220 --> 00:06:17,540
Now then, Giorno, it's on you.

73
00:06:21,060 --> 00:06:24,537
Bucerati, you're the body that we...

74
00:06:24,620 --> 00:06:25,980
back at the Coliseum.

75
00:06:26,300 --> 00:06:28,000
I don't know if it's...

76
00:06:30,540 --> 00:06:33,860
Giorno, thank you for
all that you've done.

77
00:06:34,780 --> 00:06:37,920
When you and I met for
the first time in Napoli,

78
00:06:38,660 --> 00:06:41,340
when we joined forces against the Family,

79
00:06:42,160 --> 00:06:47,460
though my body became marked for death
by Fate's hand, my soul was reborn.

80
00:06:48,680 --> 00:06:50,520
You revived my faith.

81
00:06:58,040 --> 00:07:00,393
Thank you for showing me true happiness.

82
00:07:01,280 --> 00:07:02,240
I'll be fine.

83
00:07:02,700 --> 00:07:03,800
No need to worry.

84
00:07:05,780 --> 00:07:08,240
Give everyone my regards, won't you?

85
00:07:15,340 --> 00:07:17,080
You imputant wretch!

86
00:07:17,340 --> 00:07:19,580
Such tedious bilge, all for some girl!

87
00:07:19,820 --> 00:07:22,877
You'll rot in hell, you
Philistine mounds of excrement!

88
00:07:22,960 --> 00:07:25,217
I'll be sure to send
all of you there myself!

89
00:07:25,300 --> 00:07:30,000
As soon as I conquer the arrow,
your worthless lives will be mine!

90
00:07:39,480 --> 00:07:40,560
Esu's back.

91
00:07:41,040 --> 00:07:43,140
Way to go, Bucciarati.

92
00:07:45,460 --> 00:07:47,157
Let's never do that again.

93
00:07:47,240 --> 00:07:49,299
Can't have Trish nearly died twice.

94
00:07:53,220 --> 00:07:54,900
Hey, a little help?

95
00:07:55,620 --> 00:07:58,020
I know you're worried about Bucciarati,

96
00:07:58,420 --> 00:08:02,220
but he'll be back here
before you know it, right?

97
00:08:26,160 --> 00:08:28,320
No need to fear, Jean.

98
00:08:29,460 --> 00:08:32,600
I'm simply returning to the
path I was meant to walk.

99
00:08:34,100 --> 00:08:36,080
The path to my origin.

100
00:08:37,320 --> 00:08:38,580
I'm going back.

101
00:08:39,280 --> 00:08:40,200
That's all.

102
00:09:21,660 --> 00:09:22,490
Huh?

103
00:09:22,573 --> 00:09:23,403
Benedict!

104
00:09:40,260 --> 00:09:42,360
Who was it that once said?

105
00:09:42,600 --> 00:09:46,757
We all stand as soldiers,
chosen by destiny.

106
00:09:46,840 --> 00:09:50,880
How quaint this world has
taught me other truths.

107
00:09:51,180 --> 00:09:54,057
Fate has bestowed upon me an extraordinary

108
00:09:54,140 --> 00:09:57,760
power to obliterate
time and see the future.

109
00:09:58,260 --> 00:10:02,300
As such, only one spot suits
me in the natural order.

110
00:10:03,200 --> 00:10:05,100
There is no question.

111
00:10:05,680 --> 00:10:10,800
I, Emperor Crimson, am destiny's
chosen to reign at the top.

112
00:10:11,000 --> 00:10:13,220
A mere soldier I am not!

113
00:10:13,420 --> 00:10:14,480
So why?

114
00:10:14,720 --> 00:10:16,317
Why couldn't I seize the arrow?

115
00:10:16,400 --> 00:10:18,077
It should have been so simple.

116
00:10:18,160 --> 00:10:20,631
How on earth did I fail such a small task?

117
00:10:20,920 --> 00:10:22,600
This is inconceivable.

118
00:10:23,080 --> 00:10:24,500
But it's not defeat.

119
00:10:24,740 --> 00:10:27,328
It may not be now, but
victory will be mine.

120
00:10:28,060 --> 00:10:29,920
For now, I must rest.

121
00:10:30,160 --> 00:10:33,800
I will bide my time and strike
when the moment is right.

122
00:10:34,480 --> 00:10:37,240
I haven't been beaten, only delayed.

123
00:10:37,640 --> 00:10:41,000
My powers will thrust me
back to the top in no time.

124
00:10:41,760 --> 00:10:44,540
Giorno, don't let him run. Stop him.

125
00:10:45,720 --> 00:10:50,540
If he gets away, he'll go into
Hayden, and he'll disappear.

126
00:10:51,340 --> 00:10:53,420
Once he does, we'll lose.

127
00:10:54,340 --> 00:10:58,360
Jean, I can feel him.

128
00:10:59,760 --> 00:11:01,760
He's running with his tail tucked.

129
00:11:17,180 --> 00:11:18,100
Oh, damn!

130
00:11:18,540 --> 00:11:19,500
He's holding it!

131
00:11:19,960 --> 00:11:22,607
Looks like the arrow's
picked its new master!

132
00:11:23,520 --> 00:11:24,520
Nice, Giorno!

133
00:11:26,180 --> 00:11:27,140
Damn it.

134
00:11:27,680 --> 00:11:30,820
It appears retreat was
never an option after all.

135
00:11:32,100 --> 00:11:34,120
I must face him now!

136
00:11:34,440 --> 00:11:36,420
My dignity demands it!

137
00:11:36,740 --> 00:11:38,780
You won't overthrow me!

138
00:11:39,000 --> 00:11:42,294
Try as you might, you will
never tear me from my throne!

139
00:11:42,760 --> 00:11:44,920
I won't run from you.

140
00:11:45,220 --> 00:11:47,279
That would be unbecoming of a king.

141
00:11:47,480 --> 00:11:49,160
Let's end this, now!

142
00:11:49,660 --> 00:11:52,617
When you said he was running,
which way'd you mean?

143
00:11:52,700 --> 00:11:55,277
Is he trying to take us
down with him or something?

144
00:11:55,360 --> 00:11:56,440
Golden Wind!

145
00:12:01,260 --> 00:12:02,960
All right, go Giorno!

146
00:12:03,820 --> 00:12:08,408
Suck up all that arrow's power and show
my father what Golden Wind is made of!

147
00:12:08,640 --> 00:12:09,760
Silly girl.

148
00:12:10,720 --> 00:12:13,900
No such thing will
transpire, dear daughter!

149
00:12:14,560 --> 00:12:18,540
I have to say, I'm glad your
words goaded me into staying.

150
00:12:18,900 --> 00:12:21,488
You've reminded me to
always guard my honor.

151
00:12:21,680 --> 00:12:23,440
Good thing I held my ground.

152
00:12:23,820 --> 00:12:29,040
Had I actually fled, I never would have
gotten to witness this thrilling vision.

153
00:12:36,640 --> 00:12:40,760
Thank you, Emperor Crimson
Eulogy, for this sumptuous sight.

154
00:12:41,020 --> 00:12:42,180
Golden Wind!

155
00:12:44,420 --> 00:12:45,400
All right!

156
00:12:45,680 --> 00:12:46,660
Go, Giorno!

157
00:12:46,940 --> 00:12:51,469
So come on that arrow's power and show
my father what Golden Wind is made of!

158
00:12:58,440 --> 00:13:03,000
But why it looked like it
worked what the hell happened?

159
00:13:08,120 --> 00:13:12,937
How lovely to be back on the
course of victory and right

160
00:13:13,020 --> 00:13:16,257
when I thought despair had
finally Caught me in its grip

161
00:13:16,340 --> 00:13:22,260
but the wounds you inflicted on my
pride steered me toward the right path.

162
00:13:22,620 --> 00:13:26,300
I would not have realized how
truly close I was to winning

163
00:13:27,820 --> 00:13:28,657
without you.

164
00:13:28,740 --> 00:13:32,320
Giorno Giovanna, what did
you hope to accomplish?

165
00:13:32,720 --> 00:13:35,440
The arrow won't sully
itself with the feeble?

166
00:13:35,680 --> 00:13:38,960
Did you already forget what
the detestable turtle said?

167
00:13:39,200 --> 00:13:43,180
My boy, only a worthy wielder
can lay claim to with strength.

168
00:13:43,560 --> 00:13:46,980
How glad it must be then
that I chose to stay.

169
00:13:48,200 --> 00:13:50,760
Time to die like the weakling you are!

170
00:13:50,900 --> 00:13:52,157
Don't just stand there!

171
00:13:52,240 --> 00:13:53,640
Begone, wretched dog!

172
00:13:55,420 --> 00:13:57,520
To be slain by a king!

173
00:13:57,860 --> 00:13:59,177
A final gift!

174
00:13:59,260 --> 00:14:00,560
Just all of us.

175
00:14:10,960 --> 00:14:12,360
No, Giorno.

176
00:14:12,480 --> 00:14:13,340
Wait, Mista.

177
00:14:14,180 --> 00:14:17,886
Look, there's something more than
just blood coming out of him.

178
00:14:18,020 --> 00:14:19,300
I think it worked.

179
00:14:20,040 --> 00:14:22,020
How, how did you?

180
00:14:28,420 --> 00:14:29,250
Impossible.

181
00:14:29,333 --> 00:14:30,957
This must be another trick.

182
00:14:31,040 --> 00:14:33,757
I felt his bones shattered to pieces.

183
00:14:33,840 --> 00:14:37,537
Brain matter should be spilling
from his corpse right now.

184
00:14:37,620 --> 00:14:40,297
So what is this bizarre substance?

185
00:14:40,380 --> 00:14:41,557
Don't tell me.

186
00:14:41,640 --> 00:14:43,957
Did the arrow choose him after all?

187
00:14:44,040 --> 00:14:46,700
Is that what's burrowing into his body?

188
00:14:47,760 --> 00:14:49,600
That's enough! No more!

189
00:14:49,780 --> 00:14:51,760
You die now, Giorno Javada!

190
00:14:58,040 --> 00:14:59,620
Hey, he did it!

191
00:14:59,760 --> 00:15:01,937
Giorno didn't get rejected by the arrow.

192
00:15:02,020 --> 00:15:05,377
It might have taken its time,
but turns out he was worthy.

193
00:15:05,460 --> 00:15:09,700
But it almost looks like the arrow's
become a whole new part of him.

194
00:15:10,000 --> 00:15:11,647
The boss can't take it away.

195
00:15:12,180 --> 00:15:15,474
Call me nuts, but I think
it's stuck to Giorno for good!

196
00:15:36,860 --> 00:15:39,820
What hellish nightmare has engulfed me?

197
00:15:40,160 --> 00:15:41,420
This can't be real.

198
00:15:41,620 --> 00:15:43,197
I didn't make a single mistake.

199
00:15:43,280 --> 00:15:47,440
My hand bore a hole through his
miserable skull moments ago.

200
00:15:47,740 --> 00:15:50,975
He should be on the ground,
dead, in a pool of viscera.

201
00:15:52,040 --> 00:15:53,240
It's Requiem.

202
00:15:53,540 --> 00:15:56,040
Yeah, except this time it's Giorno's.

203
00:15:56,280 --> 00:15:58,200
It's Golden Wind Requiem.

204
00:15:58,780 --> 00:16:00,620
The air around them is intense.

205
00:16:00,880 --> 00:16:03,115
They've transcended the arrow's power.

206
00:16:10,900 --> 00:16:11,730
What?

207
00:16:13,280 --> 00:16:14,110
Perfect!

208
00:16:19,640 --> 00:16:22,040
The only lasting thing is truth itself.

209
00:16:22,820 --> 00:16:24,644
Righteous actions born of truth

210
00:16:25,100 --> 00:16:26,924
will live past the end of time.

211
00:16:27,200 --> 00:16:28,700
My friends are gone,

212
00:16:29,640 --> 00:16:32,111
but I know their virtuous spirits live on.

213
00:16:32,600 --> 00:16:35,417
It was their will that the
arrow be handed down to me.

214
00:16:35,500 --> 00:16:38,780
So let's see, are your
actions founded on truth

215
00:16:39,380 --> 00:16:42,380
or are they the transient
products of shallow evil?

216
00:16:43,280 --> 00:16:45,104
I guess we'll know soon enough.

217
00:16:45,580 --> 00:16:49,860
Are you really as unbreakable as
you repeatedly claim to be, Boss?

218
00:16:50,660 --> 00:16:52,677
What the hell is he going on about?

219
00:16:52,760 --> 00:16:54,407
What's he planning on doing?

220
00:16:54,860 --> 00:16:57,620
Oh crap, please don't
swap our souls again!

221
00:16:58,080 --> 00:16:58,940
Could be that.

222
00:16:59,180 --> 00:17:00,768
Just keep your eyes peeled.

223
00:17:00,920 --> 00:17:03,437
I don't think Jorno's
really certain himself.

224
00:17:03,520 --> 00:17:04,877
But from what I can tell,

225
00:17:04,960 --> 00:17:06,757
we're not gonna have to
worry about him suddenly

226
00:17:06,840 --> 00:17:09,257
losing control over
Requiem anymore at least.

227
00:17:09,340 --> 00:17:10,811
It's nothing like before.

228
00:17:13,280 --> 00:17:14,620
I failed to see it.

229
00:17:14,760 --> 00:17:17,360
His attack managed to evade my prediction.

230
00:17:17,840 --> 00:17:21,040
No, but I did see it
coming, just not in detail.

231
00:17:21,620 --> 00:17:24,657
The vision of a projectile
bursting through my hand,

232
00:17:24,740 --> 00:17:26,622
it saved me from the full brunt.

233
00:17:27,140 --> 00:17:30,360
I can still dodge his
strikes at the last second.

234
00:17:30,840 --> 00:17:35,500
There's no question, Golden Wind's
newfound strength is nothing to scoff at.

235
00:17:35,720 --> 00:17:37,280
But that ends here.

236
00:17:37,560 --> 00:17:40,148
It's gained little more
than a harder swing.

237
00:17:40,860 --> 00:17:43,200
Emperor Crimson can still preempt him.

238
00:17:43,380 --> 00:17:45,792
There's nothing my powers can't overcome.

239
00:17:47,240 --> 00:17:50,020
Enjoy the ride while you can, dear Giorno.

240
00:17:50,460 --> 00:17:55,000
I'm coming to crush your skull
properly this time, as fate ordains.

241
00:17:55,300 --> 00:17:59,960
A little boy like you should learn to
temper his bravado, lest he's punished.

242
00:18:00,560 --> 00:18:04,501
I'll even strip you of any chance
to regret your actions, you brat.

243
00:18:04,860 --> 00:18:06,280
Go, Emperor Crimson!

244
00:18:08,460 --> 00:18:12,500
Time will now be obliterated
for all but me! Excellent!

245
00:18:12,900 --> 00:18:14,840
I can see his stance movements.

246
00:18:15,200 --> 00:18:17,940
His machinations have
been laid utterly bare.

247
00:18:23,960 --> 00:18:27,220
Talentless roaches, at
least try to surprise me.

248
00:18:29,100 --> 00:18:33,217
Amazing how little it takes to totally
neutralize your greatest power.

249
00:18:33,300 --> 00:18:36,900
Poor fools, I almost feel sorry for you.

250
00:18:37,220 --> 00:18:41,277
Never again will you witness the
immaculate brilliance of Emperor Crimson.

251
00:18:41,360 --> 00:18:44,960
The truth of my strength
will be forever lost to you.

252
00:18:47,040 --> 00:18:48,480
At last, I've won.

253
00:18:48,860 --> 00:18:50,720
In the end, I'm still faster.

254
00:18:51,220 --> 00:18:54,808
Your new powers couldn't stop
me from ripping out your heart.

255
00:18:54,920 --> 00:18:58,440
The future can only hold one
of us, and it has chosen me.

256
00:18:58,820 --> 00:19:00,160
Now disappear.

257
00:19:09,120 --> 00:19:09,950
No!

258
00:19:14,260 --> 00:19:15,460
But how?

